# A censor battery manifest. Run with:
#
#   censor libfoo.dylib --manifest etc/example.manifest \
#     --format json --attribute
#
# One dlopen, one censor/report-v3 object covering every case.

# Run-wide directives. A command-line flag overrides any of these.
meter          wall
alpha          1e-6
budget         20000
warmup         500
batch          1
target-prefix  censor_target_
workspace      128

# The sampler seed. Each case mixes its own name into this, so cases
# do not all start from identical bytes. The A/B order-bit seed is
# deliberately NOT set here: it defaults to fresh OS entropy per run,
# and the value it resolves to is reported per case, so an audit is
# randomised yet replayable.
seed           0xc0ffee5eed0beef7

# 'on' runs each of the M expanded cells at alpha/M, so the battery
# as a whole tests at alpha family-wise rather than merely reporting
# the union bound. Off by default: it costs power per cell.
family-alpha   off

# case NAME [key=value ...]
#
#   secret=off:len   pinned in class A only -- the fix-vs-random axis
#                    (repeatable; at least one is required)
#   public=off:len   pinned in BOTH classes for the whole run
#                    (repeatable)
#   context=off:len  redrawn once per PAIR, written into both classes
#                    -- one shared fresh public input per pair, so
#                    the tested axis is secret dependence given
#                    identical public bytes (repeatable)
#   workspace=N      override the run-wide workspace
#   target=SYMBOL    override target-prefix ++ NAME
#   batch=N|auto     override the run-wide batch
#   replicates=N     run N independent fixed secrets as N cases
#   label=TEXT       display name, if it should differ from NAME.
#                    Presentation only: NAME remains the case's
#                    identity, so relabelling never changes the
#                    secret a case draws.
#
# The three range roles must not overlap: a byte is pinned in class A,
# pinned in both, refreshed per pair in both, or freshly random in
# each -- never two of those at once.

case mul       secret=0:32
case ecdh      secret=0:32 context=32:64
case sign      workspace=96 secret=0:32 public=32:32

# One fixed secret answers "does *this* secret time differently from
# random". Replicating guards against an unlucky draw; each replicate
# is its own case row and counts toward the family-wise alpha.
case inv       secret=0:32 replicates=3
